      "term": "Cotton-linen blend",
      "definition": "A yarn combining cotton and linen fibres, usually in equal parts. Cotton softens the linen and adds a slight sheen; linen adds structure and keeps the fabric from going limp. The blend is washable and improves with wear."
    },
    {
      "slug": "button-band-g278",
      "term": "Button band",
      "definition": "A dc strip worked along the right and left front edges after assembly. The right band carries the buttonholes; the left band carries the buttons. Work 5 rows of dc, placing buttonholes on row 3 by working ch 1, skip 1 at each button position."
    }
